      "title": "Using Built-in Pipes",
      "lectureOrder": 165,
      "videoOrder": 157,
      "sourceHash": "51b4291e8b0572badb880a6710c17fe7af702b2c092e253abc3c1b9c3ef8a3be",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 2.25,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmüller] So where in this app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.25,
          "end": 4.74,
          "en": "could we use built-in pipes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.74,
          "end": 7.11,
          "en": "pipes that come with Angular?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.11,
          "end": 9.99,
          "en": "Well, if we take a look at the built-in pipes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.99,
          "end": 13.65,
          "en": "we can see that there are two pipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.65,
          "end": 17.4,
          "en": "that might be useful in this demo app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.4,
          "end": 20.58,
          "en": "The first interesting pipe is the DatePipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.58,
          "end": 24.39,
          "en": "which helps with formatting and outputting date values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.39,
          "end": 27.33,
          "en": "And in this app here, I got this timestamp,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.33,
          "end": 31.71,
          "en": "which is currently not output, in a very user-friendly way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.71,
          "end": 35.52,
          "en": "so that's a place where we could use a pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.52,
          "end": 37.68,
          "en": "In addition, here in this demo app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.68,
          "end": 39.45,
          "en": "we also have these numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.45,
          "end": 42.78,
          "en": "which have a lot of decimal places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.78,
          "end": 45.63,
          "en": "And here we could use the DecimalPipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.63,
          "end": 49.2,
          "en": "to change the way these numbers are displayed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.2,
          "end": 51.51,
          "en": "to only show a limited number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.51,
          "end": 54.66,
          "en": "of decimal points, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.66,
          "end": 57.06,
          "en": "And therefore, I'll start with the DatePipe here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.06,
          "end": 60.93,
          "en": "and the question is, how do we use it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.93,
          "end": 63.39,
          "en": "Well, a good place to learn more about a pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.39,
          "end": 66.36,
          "en": "is by visiting its official documentation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.36,
          "end": 69.63,
          "en": "And then here in the DatePipe in the usage notes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.63,
          "end": 72.57,
          "en": "we can see how we can configure this pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.57,
          "end": 74.97,
          "en": "and I'll get back to that in a second,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.97,
          "end": 79.08,
          "en": "but we typically also see some usage examples.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.08,
          "end": 81.87,
          "en": "Here at the bottom, we can see that we added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.87,
          "end": 84.45,
          "en": "by using such a pipe symbol",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.45,
          "end": 86.49,
          "en": "after the value that should be formatted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.49,
          "end": 90.93,
          "en": "and then we have the pipe name, date, in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.93,
          "end": 92.88,
          "en": "So back here in our example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.88,
          "end": 95.16,
          "en": "we could go to the app component template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.16,
          "end": 98.49000000000001,
          "en": "and then here where I output the currentDate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.49000000000001,
          "end": 101.37,
          "en": "we would use the built-in DatePipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.37,
          "end": 103.97999999999999,
          "en": "by adding this pipe symbol,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.97999999999999,
          "end": 106.74000000000001,
          "en": "so this vertical bar character here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.74000000000001,
          "end": 111.063,
          "en": "and then thereafter the pipe name, Date, in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.47,
          "end": 117,
          "en": "Now, just like this, it would be an unknown pipe, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 117,
          "end": 119.72999999999999,
          "en": "Angular doesn't know it automatically because,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.72999999999999,
          "end": 124.41,
          "en": "just like Components or Directives, pipes are not unlocked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.41,
          "end": 128.43,
          "en": "for all templates automatically in your Angular app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.43,
          "end": 131.16,
          "en": "Instead, if you wanna use this DatePipe here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.16,
          "end": 133.17,
          "en": "in the app component template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.17,
          "end": 136.2,
          "en": "you have to go to the app component configuration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.2,
          "end": 138.12,
          "en": "so to the decorator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.12,
          "end": 141.843,
          "en": "and add this imports array and import the DatePipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.91,
          "end": 146.67000000000002,
          "en": "And also add this import here at the top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.67000000000002,
          "end": 150.873,
          "en": "where DatePipe is imported from Angular/common.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.76,
          "end": 155.85,
          "en": "That unlocks this pipe for this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.85,
          "end": 158.523,
          "en": "and therefore now we can use it here in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 159.48,
          "end": 161.22,
          "en": "And if we use it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.22,
          "end": 165.84,
          "en": "we can see that this date now looks much better already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 165.84,
          "end": 169.8,
          "en": "But still, this might not be the way we wanna display",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 169.8,
          "end": 172.82999999999998,
          "en": "this timestamp, and that's why most pipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 172.82999999999998,
          "end": 174.243,
          "en": "can also be configured.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
